d sensibility  in her family which at the point of the  anime was given the image of being the  leaders of some warmongering empire  conquering  civilizations left and right it doesn't  help that the best of the renn family  had introductions or eventually ended up  being on the darker and more  manipulative side of things  in contrast to especially the redhead  siblings harkaway provides a much softer  edge that doesn't mean that she's weak  though  she's the character that embodies inner  strength and resolve in contrast to the  more combatable princess of the  co-empire she also dons quite the call  and badass transformation when using the  full power of her gin  speaking of idealistic and innocent  fairy tales wendy marvels at number five  who could forget sweet little wendy  always bringing a vibrant energy to the  main fairy tale cast wendy's as tough as  wind users go she may not seem like it  at first but she's the wind dragon  slayer and we know what being a dragon  slayer means in this series sure she  mainly plays a support role compared to  the other dragon slayers but where would  the whole team be without her ever since  her introductory arc wendy has played a  very important part  in practically every arc both in helping  the team in battle  or keeping the combustible elements in  the guild in line with her bubbly  personality she can kick it up a notch  in battle 2 as well with access to the  powerful dragon force she can sure pack  a punch when needed to  comes in at number four  [Music]  with the crazy things we've seen from  jojo it seems ensuing that a win-based  ability would be lackluster however this  being jojo you just know that they'll be  able to pull out something creative out  of a mundane looking ability and on a  pillar man to boot in wamu's case his  entire body becomes his weapon as he  channels the power of the wind from his  signature divine sandstorm wamu's  capable of ripping  anyone to shreds by manifesting his  power in its most destructive form using  his very body  even people like caesar have trouble  against the power of warmu's attacks  compared to the wild abilities in the  jojo universe women's wind abilities may  seem tame by comparison but that doesn't  make those abilities any less dangerous  for both his unfortunate opponents  and himself  aston's childhood friend and eternal  rival finds himself on this list because  well why wouldn't he just like aster he  seeks to become wizard king  unlike aster though yuno is naturally  talented and can be quite condescending  with his amazing wind powers manifesting  in the form of arrows and blades  it's not hard to see why he wouldn't end  up that way for me yoona really shines  in his creativity in how he combines  multiple facets of magic to become a  resourceful fighter this  is in large part to self which i can  safely say has become his ace in the  hole in a lot of situations he's also  one of those people who you would think  of as an edgy anti-hero in his first  appearances but the story quickly turns  that around and shows him in a more  sympathetic light he's one of the more  unambiguously heroic guys out there and  i think that's a pretty nice change of  pace from the sasuke characters in these  shows  just falling a bit short of the top spot  on the list is the very badass  monkey d dragon  [Music]  man  the name monkey dragon is something that  all to send chills down the spine of any  pirate hot shot in the world of one  piece and for good reason too being the  leader of the revolutionaries is one  thing but having the title of the  world's most wanted man is another  especially when we have monstrosities  like kaido  and big mom in the one-piece world look  i know bounties and titles may not mean  much when it comes to the overall  strength of the characters in one piece  but it does still say a lot about him  don't you think this is why  every scene where he appears in and  directly intervenes is treated like such  a big 